-- =====================================================================
-- Session 144 — Matt 14 extras-tier cross-references (single chapter)
-- =====================================================================
-- Adds Matt 14's extras-tier rows + threads to the cross-reference
-- corpus. Continues the S131 (Matt 1-2), S132 (Matt 3), S133 (Matt 4),
-- S134 (Matt 5), S135 (Matt 6), S137 (Matt 7-8 paired), S138 (Matt 9),
-- S139 (Matt 10), S140 (Matt 11), S142 (Matt 12), and S143 (Matt 13)
-- extras-tier coverage. Single chapter migration — Matt 14 is the
-- Eliyahu-pattern-prophet''s-death and wilderness-feeding and sea-walking
-- chapter, with the chapter''s three framework-major moments landing in
-- (a) the beheading of Yochanan (John) the Witness at Herod-Antipas''s
-- hand (vv.1-12) as the Eliyahu-pattern-prophet''s-martyrdom completing
-- the Matt 11:14 *Yochanan (John) ... is Eliyahu, which was for to come*
-- identification at the death-pattern level, with the Achav (Ahab) /
-- Yezevel (Jezebel) Tanakh-architecture recapitulating at the Herod-
-- Antipas / Herodias level; (b) the feeding-of-the-five-thousand at the
-- Galilee-desert-place (vv.13-21) as the Tanakh-recapitulation of the
-- wilderness-manna (Shemot (Exodus) 16) and Elisha''s-feeding-of-the-
-- hundred (2 Melakhim (Kings) 4:42-44) and pre-figuration of the
-- Messianic-banquet (Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 25:6), with the twelve-baskets-
-- substance signaling the twelve-tribes-restoration-architecture; and
-- (c) the walking-on-the-water (vv.22-33) as the Formed-cloud-rider''s-
-- authority-over-the-sea per the Tanakh''s direct Yahuah-substance
-- (Iyov (Job) 9:8, Tehillim (Psalm) 77:19, Habakkuk 3:15), with the
-- *be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid* (Greek *egō eimi*) speaking
-- the Tanakh''s Ehyeh-self-naming of Shemot (Exodus) 3:14 across the
-- dark water. The Gennesaret-healings at vv.34-36 close the chapter
-- with the hem-of-the-garment substance — the King wearing the Torah-
-- prescribed *tsitsit* (fringe) on the *kanaph* (corner) of his garment,
-- with the healing flowing through the kanaph enacting the Tanakh-
-- Messianic-prophecy of Malakhi (Malachi) 4:2''s *Sun of righteousness
-- arise with healing in his wings (kanaph)*. The short.md walks the
-- hem-of-the-garment substance against the inherited-Christian-Torah-
-- detached-King portrayal.
--
-- Matt 14 reading-target: the chapter walks three narrative-movements
-- with the Tanakh-substance carrying the heaviest framework-bearing
-- anchors directly (Iyov (Job) 9:8 + Psalm 77:19 + Habakkuk 3:15 for the
-- walking-on-the-sea; Shemot (Exodus) 16 + 2 Melakhim (Kings) 4:42-44 +
-- Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 25:6 for the feeding; 1 Melakhim (Kings) 16-22 +
-- 21 for the Achav-Yezevel-pattern; Bamidbar (Numbers) 15:38 + Malakhi
-- (Malachi) 4:2 for the hem-and-kanaph substance). The extras-library
-- adds five framework-bearing thread-clusters: Sirach (Ecclesiasticus)
-- 48 on Eliyahu-the-prophet''s-zeal-and-promised-return (the wisdom-
-- stream''s direct articulation of the Eliyahu-pattern Yochanan (John)
-- completes); Wisdom of Solomon 16:20-26 + 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 1:19 +
-- Sirach 24:19-22 on the wilderness-manna and the bread-from-heaven-as-
-- Word-of-Yahuah substance; Sirach 43:23-25 + Wisdom of Solomon 14:3 on
-- the wonders-of-the-sea and the Creator''s-mastery; Wisdom of Solomon
-- 18:15 + Sirach 24:3 + Wisdom of Solomon 9:1-2 on the Ehyeh-self-
-- identification and the all-powerful-Word-leaping-down-from-heaven
-- substance (the wisdom-stream''s articulation of the Formed-Word
-- proceeding from the Formless-Father, which the King''s *egō eimi* at
-- v.27 enacts at the walking-on-the-water register); Wisdom of Solomon
-- 2:10-20 on the ungodly-determining-to-lie-in-wait-for-and-condemn-the-
-- righteous-with-shameful-death (THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor
-- for the disposition Herod-Antipas / Herodias / Salome enact at
-- vv.3-12). 1 Enoch and Jubilees do not surface framework-bearing
-- Matt 14 connections at S144 (the chapter''s substance is narrative-
-- enactment of Tanakh-Yahuah-pattern rather than wisdom-stream-mythos
-- territory). Sonnini''s Acts of Paul, Ascension of Isaiah, Apocalypse
-- of Abraham, Adam-Eve Conflict, and Jasher do not surface framework-
-- bearing Matt 14 connections at S144. Historical-witness editions
-- (Josephus, M.R. James''s apocryphal NT, Lightfoot''s Apostolic
-- Fathers) remain deferred from V1 cross-refs per the historical-
-- witness one-way rule. The lookup view retains the full S139 edition
-- set for forward compatibility.
--
-- Five PROPOSED threads at extras-tier:
--   1. `eliyahu-prophet-pattern-and-promised-return-in-sirach-48`                                   (sort 292)
--   2. `wilderness-manna-and-bread-as-word-in-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras-and-sirach`            (sort 293)
--   3. `wonders-of-the-sea-and-the-creators-mastery-in-sirach-and-wisdom-of-solomon`                (sort 294)
--   4. `ehyeh-self-identification-and-the-all-powerful-word-from-heaven-in-wisdom-and-sirach`       (sort 295)
--   5. `righteous-witness-lied-in-wait-for-and-condemned-with-shameful-death-in-wisdom-of-solomon`  (sort 296)
--
-- 17 new cross_references rows at tier_required=''extras'' (Library tier,
-- $4.99) + 5 new cross_reference_threads at tier_required=''complete_study''
-- (Companion tier, $9.99). The tier split honors the two-layer
-- architecture of the chapter-end card: Layer 1 (per-verse cross-refs)
-- visible to Library readers who have access to the extras-library
-- editions the refs point to; Layer 2 (framework thread callouts with
-- summary_md + member_notes) gated at Companion, since the threads ARE
-- the framework''s reading of how canon and library answer each other —
-- the "hidden detail expand" that is the Companion-tier upgrade. Every
-- member-note passes the 12 Red Lines and the 12-point editorial
-- checklist. Hebrew names with internal apostrophes (Yashar''el,
-- Ya''aqov, Yechezk''el, Yo''el, Sha''ul, Mikha''el, Gavri''el,
-- Shemu''el, Mosheh''s, King''s, Father''s, Yahuah''s, Yochanan''s, etc.)
-- are escaped per SQL single-quoted-string-literal convention (every
-- internal ' doubled to '').
--
-- Idempotent: ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING on every INSERT.
-- =====================================================================

\echo 'Session 144 — Matt 14 extras-tier cross-references migration starting...'
BEGIN;

-- Verse-lookup temp view. Mirrors the S143 view including
-- `sonnini-acts-29`; retained for forward compatibility even though
-- Matt 14 does not surface a Sonnini Acts 29 connection at S144.
CREATE TEMP VIEW _s144_verse_lookup AS
SELECT
    e.slug AS edition_slug,
    b.slug AS book_slug,
    c.chapter_number,
    v.verse_number,
    v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v
  JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id
  JOIN books    b ON c.book_id    = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN (
       'canon',
       'enoch',
       'jubilees',
       'jasher',
       'apocrypha',
       'apocrypha-charles-vol1',
       'pseudepigrapha',
       'adam-eve-conflict',
       'apocalypse-of-abraham',
       'ascension-isaiah',
       'sonnini-acts-29'
   );

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Insert 17 extras-tier cross_references rows.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------
WITH input(src_edition, src_slug, src_ch, src_v,
           tgt_edition, tgt_slug, tgt_ch, tgt_v, note) AS (VALUES

  -- Thread 1: eliyahu-prophet-pattern-and-promised-return-in-sirach-48
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 3, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 1,
   '*Then stood up Eliyahu (Elias) the prophet as fire, and his word burned like a lamp.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Eliyahu-pattern prophet''s-fiery-zeal-at-the-royal-court architecture: the prophet stood-up-as-fire and his word burned-like-a-lamp. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:3-4''s *Herod had laid hold on Yochanan (John), and bound him ... For Yochanan (John) said unto him, It is not lawful for thee to have her.* Yochanan (John)''s confrontation of Herod-Antipas at the Torah-violation operates in the same Eliyahu-pattern the wisdom-stream had named at the Achav (Ahab)-confrontation register. The Matt 11:14 identification of Yochanan (John) as *Eliyahu, which was for to come* is corroborated at the prophet''s-zeal-and-Torah-confrontation pattern Sirach 48 walks. The wisdom-stream knew the architecture; Matt 14 names the operative-form at the gospel-level.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 3, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 2,
   '*Who brought a sore famine upon them, and by his zeal he diminished their number.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:2 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Eliyahu-pattern prophet''s-zeal-bringing-judgment-on-the-Torah-violators substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:3-5''s Yochanan (John)''s confrontation of Herod-Antipas''s Torah-violation: the Eliyahu-pattern prophet''s-zeal at the Achav-Yezevel Torah-violation produced the famine-judgment (1 Melakhim (Kings) 17:1); Yochanan (John)''s-zeal at the Herod-Herodias Torah-violation produces the imprisonment-and-eventual-martyrdom. The Tanakh-pattern of the Eliyahu-pattern prophet''s-confrontation-of-the-unrighteous-ruler the wisdom-stream had named the architecture for; Matt 14 names the operative-form at the second-coming-of-Eliyahu (the first-coming, preparing for the King''s-first-arrival).'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 5, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 10,
   '*Who wast ordained for reproofs in their times, to pacify the wrath of Yahuah (the Lord''s) judgment, before it brake forth into fury, and to turn the heart of the father unto the son, and to restore the tribes of Ya''aqov (Jacob).* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:10 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the Malakhi (Malachi) 4:5-6 Eliyahu-promised-return substance: Eliyahu shall-be-ordained-for-reproofs and turn-the-heart-of-the-father-unto-the-son and restore-the-tribes-of-Ya''aqov (Jacob). The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:5''s *they counted him as a prophet* — the Galilee-multitudes recognized Yochanan (John) as the Eliyahu-pattern-prophet the wisdom-stream had named the architecture for. The Matt 11:14 identification (*if ye will receive it, this is Eliyahu, which was for to come*) operates in the same architecture Sirach 48:10 had named. The framework reads the architecture in two-fold structure per voice-skill''s eschatological-architecture: Yochanan (John) was the first-Eliyahu-coming preparing-the-way for the first-coming-of-the-King; the eschatological-second-Eliyahu (one of the two-witnesses of Revelation 11) will prepare for the second-coming. The restoration-of-the-tribes-of-Ya''aqov (Jacob) substance of Sirach 48:10 is the framework''s scattered-seed-gathering-architecture the wisdom-stream knew.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 12, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 48, 11,
   '*Blessed are they that saw thee, and slept in love; for we shall surely live.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 48:11 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Eliyahu-pattern prophet''s-disciples-blessed-in-the-prophet''s-departure substance. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:12''s *and his disciples came, and took up the body, and buried it, and went and told Yahusha (Jesus).* The Eliyahu-pattern-prophet''s-disciples honor the departing-prophet (Sirach 48:11 in the chariot-translation register; Yochanan (John)''s disciples at the burial-after-the-beheading) and walk-forward into the One the prophet prepared-the-way-for. The wisdom-stream knew the architecture of the prophet''s-disciples-blessed-and-living-onward; Matt 14:12 names the operative-form at the gospel-pivot-from-Yochanan (John)-to-Yahusha (Jesus). The disciples'' going-to-tell-Yahusha (Jesus) is the seed-war-pattern operating in the gathering-direction — Yochanan (John)''s-faithful-disciples drawn-into-the-King''s-orbit.'),

  -- Thread 2: wilderness-manna-and-bread-as-word-in-wisdom-of-solomon-and-2-esdras-and-sirach
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 13, 'apocrypha', '2-esdras', 1, 19,
   '*I gave you angels'' food to eat in your hunger; and when ye thirsted, I clave the rock, and waters flowed out to your fill.* 2 Esdras (4 Ezra) 1:19 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father''s-wilderness-feeding-of-the-multitude architecture: angels''-food in the hunger; water-from-the-rock in the thirst. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:13-14''s King-withdrawing-into-the-desert-place and the multitudes-following-on-foot. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the Father''s-wilderness-feeding through the Mosheh (Moses)-mediated-manna; the King at Matt 14:13-21 enacts the same architecture in person at the Galilee-desert-place. The Father''s-wilderness-feeding-of-the-multitude operates across the canon and the wisdom-stream as one architecture; the King recapitulates the substance without mediation in the chapter''s feeding-pericope.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 19, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 16, 20,
   '*Instead whereof thou feddest thine own people with angels'' food, and didst send them from heaven bread prepared without their labour, able to content every man''s delight, and agreeing to every taste.* Wisdom of Solomon 16:20 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the wilderness-manna substance: the Father fed-his-own-people with angels''-food sent-them-from-heaven bread-prepared-without-their-labour. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:19''s King-taking-the-loaves-and-fishes and looking-up-to-heaven and blessing-and-breaking-and-distributing. The Father''s-bread-from-heaven of Wisdom 16:20 is the substance the King enacts at the Galilee-desert-place — bread-prepared-without-their-labour multiplied for the multitudes, with the disciples-as-the-distribution-channel. The wisdom-stream knew the architecture; the King names the operative-form at the gospel-register; the John 6 *I am the bread of life* discourse following the Yochanan (John)-account of this same feeding-pericope (John 6:1-15 + 6:35) locks the substance: the King IS the bread-from-heaven the wisdom-stream had named the Father-feeding-his-people-with.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 19, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 16, 26,
   '*That thy children, O Yahuah (Lord), whom thou lovest, might know that it is not the growing of fruits that nourisheth man: but that it is thy word, which preserveth them that put their trust in thee.* Wisdom of Solomon 16:26 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the bread-of-life-is-the-Word-of-Yahuah substance: not-the-growing-of-fruits-nourisheth-man but-thy-Word-preserveth-them-that-trust. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:19''s feeding-of-the-five-thousand and the Word-of-the-King the disciples have been receiving across the gospel. The wisdom-stream had named the substance the King anchors in the Yochanan (John) 6 account directly: *it is the spirit that quickeneth; the flesh profiteth nothing: the words that I speak unto you, they are spirit, and they are life* (John 6:63). The feeding-substance points beyond-the-loaves to the Word-of-the-King the disciples are being trained to receive as the bread-from-heaven the wisdom-stream had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 20, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 24, 19,
   '*Come unto me, all ye that be desirous of me, and fill yourselves with my fruits.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 24:19 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the wisdom-feeding-her-children-with-her-fruits architecture: come-unto-me and fill-yourselves-with-my-fruits. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:20''s *and they did all eat, and were filled.* The wisdom-stream knew the architecture of the wisdom-feeding-and-filling at the come-unto-me register; the King at Matt 14:20 enacts the operative-form at the Galilee-desert-place: the multitudes come; they eat; they are filled. The framework reads the Sirach 24:19 anchor in continuity with Matt 11:28''s *come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest* — the King''s come-unto-me invitation across his ministry is the operative-form of the wisdom-stream''s wisdom-inviting substance. The twelve-baskets-leftover of v.20 signal the twelve-tribes-restoration-architecture the wisdom-of-the-most-High had named as the destination-substance: the wisdom''s-children gathered-and-fed in the wilderness.'),

  -- Thread 3: wonders-of-the-sea-and-the-creators-mastery-in-sirach-and-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 25, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 43, 23,
   '*By his counsel he appeaseth the deep, and planteth islands therein.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 43:23 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Creator''s-appeasing-the-deep architecture: by-his-counsel he-appeaseth-the-deep. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:25''s King-walking-on-the-sea in the fourth-watch. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture-of-the-Creator''s-mastery-of-the-deep at the counsel-and-appeasing register; the King enacts the operative-form by walking on the very-substance the Creator-masters. The Tanakh-direct-substance of Iyov (Job) 9:8 (*which alone spreadeth out the heavens, and treadeth upon the waves of the sea*) names the action; the wisdom-stream''s Sirach 43:23 names the authority-behind-the-action; the King at Matt 14:25 enacts both at once. The Formed-cloud-rider acts in the substance the Formless-Father''s-counsel established.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 25, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 43, 25,
   '*For in it be strange and wondrous works, variety of all kinds of beasts and whales created.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 43:25 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the wonders-of-the-sea architecture: the sea-contains the strange-and-wondrous-works of the Creator. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:25-27''s walking-on-the-sea in the fourth-watch with the *it is I* self-identification. The wisdom-stream had named the substance of the sea-as-the-Creator''s-domain; the King at Matt 14:25 walks the sea AS the Creator-of-the-sea, with the *egō eimi* of v.27 naming the speaker as the One whose-counsel-appeases-the-deep at Sirach 43:23. The substance the wisdom-stream had named at the Creator-register operates in the King''s-walking-and-naming at the gospel-register.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 25, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 14, 3,
   '*But thy providence, O Father, governeth it: for thou hast made a way in the sea, and a safe path in the waves.* Wisdom of Solomon 14:3 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father''s-providence-governing-the-sea architecture: the Father''s-providence governs-the-sea and makes-a-way-in-the-sea-and-a-safe-path-in-the-waves. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:25''s King-walking-on-the-sea making-a-way-on-the-waves toward-the-disciples-in-the-tossed-ship. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the Father''s-way-in-the-sea (echoing Tehillim (Psalm) 77:19 — *thy way is in the sea, and thy path in the great waters*); the King at Matt 14:25 enacts the operative-form of the same architecture. The Formed-Son walks the way the Formless-Father''s-providence-makes-in-the-sea — and the King''s catch-of-Kefa (Peter) at v.31 is the safe-path-in-the-waves the wisdom-stream had named the Father-providing-for-the-traveler.'),

  -- Thread 4: ehyeh-self-identification-and-the-all-powerful-word-from-heaven-in-wisdom-and-sirach
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 27, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 18, 15,
   '*Thine almighty word leaped down from heaven out of thy royal throne, as a fierce man of war into the midst of a land of destruction.* Wisdom of Solomon 18:15 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the all-powerful-Word-leaping-down-from-heaven substance: thine-almighty-Word leaped-down-from-heaven out-of-thy-royal-throne. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:27''s *be of good cheer; it is I; be not afraid* — the King''s *egō eimi* self-identification at the walking-on-the-sea moment. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the all-powerful-Word from-the-Father''s-throne-coming-down-from-heaven; the Yochanan (John) 1:14 *the Word was made flesh, and dwelt among us* names the substance-in-person; the King''s *it is I* across the dark water at the fourth-watch is the operative-form of the Word-from-heaven the wisdom-stream had named. The Formed-Word that proceeded from the Formless-Father in the Wisdom 18:15 architecture is the speaker walking-on-the-water and naming-himself with the Ehyeh-substance of Shemot (Exodus) 3:14.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 27, 'apocrypha', 'ecclesiasticus', 24, 3,
   '*I came out of the mouth of the most High, and covered the earth as a cloud.* Sirach (Ecclesiasticus) 24:3 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Wisdom-proceeding-from-the-mouth-of-the-most-High architecture: came-out-of-the-mouth-of-the-most-High and covered-the-earth-as-a-cloud. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:27''s *it is I* (*egō eimi*) — the King''s self-naming with the Ehyeh-substance. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the Formed-substance proceeding from-the-mouth-of-the-Formless-most-High; the King at Matt 14:27 names-himself in the same substance the wisdom-stream had identified as the Wisdom-from-the-mouth-of-the-most-High. The framework reads this in continuity with the Yochanan (John) 8:58 *before Avraham (Abraham) was, I am* — the King''s direct Ehyeh-substance self-identification operates in the architecture the wisdom-stream knew at the Wisdom-proceeding-from-the-Father register. The Formed-Word the Father spoke is the speaker on the water; the cloud-covering-the-earth substance is the cloud-rider Tanakh-substance the Tanakh-prophets had named.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 27, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 9, 1,
   '*O Elohim (God) of my fathers, and Yahuah (Lord) of mercy, who hast made all things with thy word.* Wisdom of Solomon 9:1 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the Father-made-all-things-with-his-Word architecture: the Father has-made-all-things-with-his-Word. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:27''s *it is I* and the walking-on-the-sea moment of v.25. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture of the Word-as-the-Father''s-agent-of-creation; the King at Matt 14:25-27 walks-on-the-sea (the creation-substance) AS the Word-through-whom-all-things-were-made (per Yochanan (John) 1:3 — *all things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made*). The framework reads the substance in continuity: the Father''s-Word who made-all-things at Wisdom 9:1 + the Word-was-made-flesh at John 1:14 + the King-walking-on-the-sea-and-naming-himself-Ehyeh at Matt 14:25-27 = one architecture of the Formed-Word the Formless-Father expressed-from-the-beginning, now-walking-in-the-flesh on the sea his-own-Word-created.'),

  -- Thread 5: righteous-witness-lied-in-wait-for-and-condemned-with-shameful-death-in-wisdom-of-solomon
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 3, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 12,
   '*Therefore let us lie in wait for the righteous; because he is not for our turn, and he is clean contrary to our doings: he upbraideth us with our offending the law, and objecteth to our infamy the transgressings of our education.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:12 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the ungodly-determining-to-lie-in-wait-for-the-righteous architecture: the ungodly determine to-lie-in-wait-for-the-righteous because-he-is-clean-contrary-to-our-doings and upbraideth-us-with-our-offending-the-Torah. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:3-4''s Herod-laying-hold-on-Yochanan (John) and binding-him for Herodias''s-sake because Yochanan (John) said *it is not lawful for thee to have her.* Yochanan (John) upbraided Herod with the Torah-violation; Herod-Herodias determined to-lie-in-wait-for-the-righteous and to-bind-him. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture-of-the-ungodly-disposition-toward-the-Torah-upbraiding-prophet centuries before; Matt 14:3-12 names the operative-form at the Herod-Antipas / Herodias / Salome arrangement. The disposition the wisdom-stream named operates at every recurrence of the architecture — the Pharisees against the King at Matt 12:14, Herod-Antipas against Yochanan (John) at Matt 14:3-12, the Sanhedrin against the King at Matt 26:3-4.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 5, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 19,
   '*Let us examine him with despitefulness and torture, that we may know his meekness, and prove his patience.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:19 names the wisdom-stream''s direct articulation of the ungodly-determining-to-examine-the-righteous-with-despitefulness-and-torture architecture: examine-him-with-despitefulness-and-torture that-we-may-know-his-meekness. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:5''s Herod''s-restraint-from-killing-Yochanan-because-of-the-multitude — the disposition is to-test-and-eventually-kill, restrained-only-by-political-calculation. The wisdom-stream had named the architecture; Matt 14:5 names the operative-restraint-mechanism (the multitude''s-fear) the disposition operates-within until the birthday-banquet arrangement removes the restraint. The framework reads the architecture in continuity with the Yeshayahu (Isaiah) 53:7 *as a sheep before her shearers is dumb, so he openeth not his mouth* substance — the meekness-and-patience the ungodly-determine-to-examine-and-prove operates in the same architecture across Yochanan (John)''s-imprisonment, the King''s-trial, and the apostolic-band''s persecutions in Acts.'),
  ('canon', 'matthew', 14, 10, 'apocrypha', 'the-wisdom-of-solomon', 2, 20,
   '*Let us condemn him with a shameful death: for by his own saying he shall be respected.* Wisdom of Solomon 2:20 names THE direct wisdom-stream verbal-anchor for the ungodly-determining-to-condemn-the-righteous-with-a-shameful-death architecture: condemn-him-with-a-shameful-death. The framework reads the verse against Matt 14:10''s *and he sent, and beheaded Yochanan (John) in the prison.* The shameful-death of the wisdom-stream''s articulation is the beheading-in-the-prison the operative-form: the death is not the honorable-end of the natural-life-span; it is the execution-at-the-arrangement-of-the-corrupted-court at the birthday-banquet-oath. The framework reads the architecture in continuity with the broader Tanakh-prophet-killing pattern (2 Chronicles 24:20-22; Matt 23:34-37) — the shameful-deaths the ungodly-arrange for the Torah-upbraiding-prophets walk one architecture across the canon, the wisdom-stream, and the gospel-of-the-King''s-ministry.')

)
INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, 'extras'::content_tier
  FROM input i
  JOIN _s144_verse_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug = i.src_edition
                            AND sv.book_slug    = i.src_slug
                            AND sv.chapter_number = i.src_ch
                            AND sv.verse_number  = i.src_v
  JOIN _s144_verse_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug = i.tgt_edition
                            AND tv.book_slug    = i.tgt_slug
                            AND tv.chapter_number = i.tgt_ch
                            AND tv.verse_number  = i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

